    buf_bytes(out, b"the entry; `e.path()`), `fs::exists(p)?` (a `Result<bool>`). Errors are\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`io::Error` (`e.kind()`, an `ErrorKind`; Display as Rust's: `No such file\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"or directory (os error 2)`), and `io::Result<T>` goes with `?`; `main`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"returns an `i32`, so a `run() -> io::Result<()>` does the work.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`BufReader::new(f)` and `BufWriter::new(f)` keep their buffer inline (no\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"allocation). With `use std::io::BufRead`, `r.read_line(&mut s)?` appends a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"line, its `'\\n'` included (0 at the end), and `r.lines_in(gpa)` yields\n");
